<section id="A0.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A0.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">-A</span> </span><span id="A0.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Supplementary results for the independence assumption investigations in Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="IV-A Independence assumption ‣ IV Analysis: quantifying uncertainty ‣ Towards Reliable and Practical LLM Security Evaluations via Bayesian Modelling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-A</span></a></span></h3>

<figure id="A0.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.05709v1/figures/appendix_embeddings_analysis.png" id="A0.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:381/499;" width="381" height="499" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 5: </span>Visualisation of the prompts from each attack. From left to right: (1) embedding when PCA is applied, (2) embedding when t-SNE is applied, and (3) the scree plot.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A0.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">-B</span> </span><span id="A0.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof and derivation of importance sampling procedure</span></h3>

<div id="A0.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We derive the importance sampling procedure described in Section <a href="#S4.SS3" title="IV-C Implementation ‣ IV Analysis: quantifying uncertainty ‣ Towards Reliable and Practical LLM Security Evaluations via Bayesian Modelling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-C</span></a> in full. Firstly, we note that the target distribution for an attack <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})</annotation></semantics></math>. To show that the importance sampling procedure results in weighted samples from this distribution, we first show that the procedure targets the distribution <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})</annotation></semantics></math> and then that the distribution for <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> is the result of marginalising over this extended space. First, the joint distribution for <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</p>
<table id="A0.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})\propto p(S)p(p_{1:S}|x_{1:n},S)p(x_{1:n}|S)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})\propto p(S)p(p_{1:S}|x_{1:n},S)p(x_{1:n}|S).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since the mapping from the number of clusters to cluster assignments is deterministic, sampling from this distribution amounts to sampling <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> from its prior, <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(S)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{1:S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1:S}</annotation></semantics></math> from the conditional distribution <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(p_{1:S}|x_{1:n},S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(p_{1:S}|x_{1:n},S)</annotation></semantics></math> and weighting these samples according to the marginal likelihood, <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(x_{1:n}|S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x_{1:n}|S)</annotation></semantics></math>. Sampling from the prior is immediate and it is fairly easy to show that <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(p_{1:S}|x_{1:n},S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(p_{1:S}|x_{1:n},S)</annotation></semantics></math> amounts to sampling from separate Beta distributions due independence and the Beta-Binomial distribution conjugacy. Specifically, given the model in Section <a href="#S4" title="IV Analysis: quantifying uncertainty ‣ Towards Reliable and Practical LLM Security Evaluations via Bayesian Modelling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A0.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{k}|x_{1:n},S\sim\text{Beta}(1+\sum_{i\in C_{k}}x_{i},1+\sum_{i\in C_{k}}(m_{i}-x_{i}))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>∼</mo><mtext>Beta</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}|x_{1:n},S\sim\text{Beta}(1+\sum_{i\in C_{k}}x_{i},1+\sum_{i\in C_{k}}(m_{i}-x_{i})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">for <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in{1,\dots,S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in{1,\dots,S}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given that we have these sampling schemes, we now derive an expression for the weights using the marginal likelihood. First, the marginal likelihood can be expressed as the integral over <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{1:S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1:S}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A0.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A0.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p(x_{1:n}|S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(x_{1:n}|S)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int p(p_{1:S}|S)p(x_{1:n}|p_{1:S},S)dp_{1:S}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int p(p_{1:S}|S)p(x_{1:n}|p_{1:S},S)dp_{1:S},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{k=1}^{S}\frac{1}{\beta(1,1)}\Big(\prod_{i\in\mathcal{C}_{k}}{m_{i}\choose x_{i}}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{k=1}^{S}\frac{1}{\beta(1,1)}\Big(\prod_{i\in\mathcal{C}_{k}}{m_{i}\choose x_{i}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\quad\times\int p_{k}^{\sum x_{i}}(1-p_{k})^{\sum(m_{i}-x_{i})}dp_{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub></mrow></mstyle></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">m</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mstyle></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\quad\times\int p_{k}^{\sum x_{i}}(1-p_{k})^{\sum(m_{i}-x_{i})}dp_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">due to the distributional independence in the <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, since the integral in the second line of Equation (<a href="#A0.E2" title="In -B Proof and derivation of importance sampling procedure ‣ Towards Reliable and Practical LLM Security Evaluations via Bayesian Modelling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) corresponds to the normalising constant of a Beta distribution, we have that</p>
<table id="A0.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A0.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p(x_{1:n}|S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(x_{1:n}|S)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{k=1}^{S}\frac{1}{\beta(1,1)}\Big(\prod_{i\in\mathcal{C}_{k}}{m_{i}\choose x_{i}}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{k=1}^{S}\frac{1}{\beta(1,1)}\Big(\prod_{i\in\mathcal{C}_{k}}{m_{i}\choose x_{i}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\quad\times\beta(1+\sum_{i\in\mathcal{C}_{k}}x_{i},1+\sum_{i\in\mathcal{C}_{k}}(m_{i}-x_{i}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\quad\times\beta(1+\sum_{i\in\mathcal{C}_{k}}x_{i},1+\sum_{i\in\mathcal{C}_{k}}(m_{i}-x_{i})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Beta function. We can evaluate this marginal likelihood to calculate the weights up to proportionality and normalise so that they sum to one. Calculating these weights for the samples described, i.e. the first steps of our importance sampling procedure in Section <a href="#S4.SS3" title="IV-C Implementation ‣ IV Analysis: quantifying uncertainty ‣ Towards Reliable and Practical LLM Security Evaluations via Bayesian Modelling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-C</span></a>, we draw weighted Monte Carlo samples directly from <math id="A0.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now show that the target posterior, <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})</annotation></semantics></math>, is the result of marginalising over an extended space including the cluster-wise probabilities and the number of clusters, thus we can formulate a Monte Carlo approximation <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})</annotation></semantics></math>. We can write <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})</annotation></semantics></math> as the marginal of the joint distribution with the number of clusters, <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, and the associated cluster probabilities, <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{1:S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1:S}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A0.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})=\sum_{S=1}^{n}\int p(p_{a},p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})dp_{1:S}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mo>∫</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})=\sum_{S=1}^{n}\int p(p_{a},p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})dp_{1:S}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This can be written as</p>
<table id="A0.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A0.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{S=1}^{n}\int p(p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})p(p_{a}|p_{1:S},S,x_{1:n})dp_{1:S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{S=1}^{n}\int p(p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})p(p_{a}|p_{1:S},S,x_{1:n})dp_{1:S}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{S=1}^{n}\int p(p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})\delta_{p_{a}}(\frac{1}{S}\sum_{k=1}^{S}p_{k})dp_{1:S}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{S=1}^{n}\int p(p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})\delta_{p_{a}}(\frac{1}{S}\sum_{k=1}^{S}p_{k})dp_{1:S},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">noting that, since <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> is deterministic given <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{1:S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1:S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write its probability distribution given <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{1:S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1:S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> as a delta function. Given <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> weighted Monte Carlo samples, <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{(p_{1:S}^{t},S^{t}),W^{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(p_{1:S}^{t},S^{t}),W^{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, from <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(p_{1:S},S|x_{1:n})</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write</p>
<table id="A0.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A0.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(p_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(p_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle|x_{1:n})\approx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≈</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|x_{1:n})\approx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{S=1}^{n}\int\sum_{t=1}^{T}W^{t}\delta_{p_{a}}(\frac{1}{S^{t}}\sum_{k=1}^{S^{t}}p_{k}^{t})\delta_{(p_{1:S},S)}(p_{1:S}^{t},S^{t})dp_{1:S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{S=1}^{n}\int\sum_{t=1}^{T}W^{t}\delta_{p_{a}}(\frac{1}{S^{t}}\sum_{k=1}^{S^{t}}p_{k}^{t})\delta_{(p_{1:S},S)}(p_{1:S}^{t},S^{t})dp_{1:S}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A0.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\implies p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})=\sum_{t=1}^{T}W^{t}\delta_{p_{a}}(\frac{1}{S^{t}}\sum_{k=1}^{S^{t}}p_{k}^{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></munderover><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\implies p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})=\sum_{t=1}^{T}W^{t}\delta_{p_{a}}(\frac{1}{S^{t}}\sum_{k=1}^{S^{t}}p_{k}^{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">thus taking the average cluster-wise probabilities with weights <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W^{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> approximates the target posterior. That is, if <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{a}^{t}=\frac{1}{S^{t}}\sum_{k=1}^{S}p_{k}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{a}^{t}=\frac{1}{S^{t}}\sum_{k=1}^{S}p_{k}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\dots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\dots,T</annotation></semantics></math>, then the weighted samples <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{a}^{t},W^{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{a}^{t},W^{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> approximate <math id="A0.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(p_{a}|x_{1:n})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A0.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">-C</span> </span><span id="A0.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Supplementary results for the model validation in Section <a href="#S5.SS4" title="V-D Results ‣ V Bayesian model validation ‣ Towards Reliable and Practical LLM Security Evaluations via Bayesian Modelling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">V-D</span></a></span></h3>

<figure id="A0.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.05709v1/figures/prompt_heatmap_mamba-2.8b-hf.png" id="A0.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:720/616;" width="720" height="616" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 6: </span>Cluster label PSMs for each attack and the 2.8b parameter Mamba model. Labels on the x axis appear in the same order as those on the y axis and the results are pre-processed by hierarchical clustering on the label orders for presentational purposes.</figcaption>
</figure>
